\code{\link[=sync_sp_list_columns]{sync_sp_list_columns()}} applies those changes. By default, it only prints
the planned changes (\code{dry_run = TRUE}) and doesn't delete columns
(\code{delete = FALSE}).
}
\details{
Comparing columns

Columns are matched by internal name (\code{name}). Only the properties included
in a definition are compared, so a definition with \code{text: {}} matches any
text column. A property missing from a definition isn't changed.

SharePoint internal columns and the \code{Title} column are excluded unless
\code{Title} is included in the definitions. Columns in the list that aren't in
the definitions are returned with \code{action = "delete"}.

Each change has one of these actions:
\itemize{
\item \code{"add"}: the column isn't in the list.
\item \code{"update"}: a property is different.
\item \code{"delete"}: the column isn't in the definitions.
\item \code{"blocked"}: the change can't be made. This includes changing the column
type (e.g. text to number), changing a lookup column's source list, and
adding a column type the Graph API can't create.
\item \code{"unverified"}: the current value can't be read with the Graph API. This
includes \code{validation} (which \code{\link[=sync_sp_list_columns]{sync_sp_list_columns()}} applies every time)
and columns where the Graph API doesn't return the column type
(hyperlink, picture, thumbnail, and term columns).
}

A column's internal name can't be changed. A renamed column is returned as
a column to add and a column to delete.

If \code{sp_list} is a \code{ms_list} object and \code{definitions} is a list definition,
the list \code{displayName}, \code{description}, and \code{list} settings (\code{hidden} and
\code{contentTypesEnabled}) are also compared. These changes have a missing
\code{name}. A different \code{template} is blocked since the template can't be
changed after a list is created.

Changes that use the SharePoint REST API

SharePoint stores single and multiple lines of text and single and multiple
choice columns as different field types, and the Graph API can't change
them. These changes use the SharePoint REST API (\code{method = "rest"}):
\itemize{
\item \code{text.allowMultipleLines}: switching to multiple lines keeps existing
values. Switching to a single line truncates values longer than 255
characters, so it is skipped unless \code{allow_data_loss = TRUE}.
\item \code{choice.displayAs} to or from \code{"checkBoxes"}: switching to multiple
choice keeps existing values. Switching to a single choice may drop
values from items with more than one choice, so it is skipped unless
\code{allow_data_loss = TRUE}.
\item \code{validation}: the Graph API can't create or update column validation.
}

The SharePoint REST API requires a delegated (user) login with a refresh
token, such as the default Microsoft365R login.
